# Line-ending policy for this repo. It is NOT a fork of an upstream project -
# origin is the only remote - so there is no sync to stay byte-close to, and the
# earlier "conservative, do not normalise" policy (copied from the
# Delphi-Cross-Socket fork, where it IS correct) only produced an inconsistent
# index. Pascal sources are pinned below; force endings anywhere a wrong one
# breaks the file, and keep byte-exact files intact.

# Scripts & CI — a wrong ending breaks these
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.bat    text eol=crlf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
*.ps1    text eol=crlf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf

# Patches & diffs — never normalise; stay identical to source
*.patch  -text
*.diff   -text

# Certs / keys — exact bytes
*.crt binary
*.cer binary
*.der binary
*.pem binary
*.key binary
*.pfx binary
*.p12 binary

# Binaries / build artifacts
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.res binary
*.dcr binary
*.dcu binary
*.dcp binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so  binary
*.dylib binary

# Pascal sources — LF in the repository, CRLF in the working tree.
#
# Previously unlisted and left to core.autocrlf, which produced a SPLIT INDEX: 34
# files stored LF, 13 stored CRLF, 4 LF in both. Editing one of the CRLF-stored
# minority made autocrlf renormalise the whole file, so a real +157/-1 change to
# Horse.Provider.CrossSocket.Server.pas was committed as 2138 insertions /
# 1001 deletions and had to be reset and redone (2026-09-28, v1.0.25).
#
# text=auto rather than plain text, matching horse-provider-mormot and
# horse-provider-ics: it lets git's own heuristic skip anything it reads as binary,
# so a UTF-16 source could never be corrupted by normalisation. There are none
# today - checked - which is exactly why the guard should be in place before one
# appears. *.inc is listed for the same reason: zero files match right now.
*.pas    text=auto eol=crlf
*.dpr    text=auto eol=crlf
*.inc    text=auto eol=crlf

# NOTE: *.dproj is deliberately still NOT listed. The Delphi IDE owns those files
#       and CLAUDE.md forbids editing them, so they are left to core.autocrlf
#       rather than renormalised by a commit no IDE asked for.
